# JetonBro operating contract

Before planning, editing, running commands, or responding to any implementation request, read the root `.cursorfile` completely.

Treat `.cursorfile` as the living operating contract for this repository.

After every accepted change, update `.cursorfile` if the change affects architecture, product boundaries, state transitions, accounting rules, permissions, data ownership, skin structure, testing requirements, deployment commands, current implementation status, or the next agreed milestone.

Never silently bypass, weaken, delete, or contradict `.cursorfile`. If a requested change conflicts with it, stop and explain the conflict before editing.
